  "content": {
    "text": "5 days ago\nSouth Korea stocks endure more volatility\nThe whipsaw action in South Korean stocks continued on Wednesday. After diving 8.3% on Monday, jumping 8.2% on Tuesday, the Kospi index in Seoul saw a 4.5% fall in the latest session.\nThe South Korean market remains up 166% over the last 12 months, buoyed in the main by strength in chip stocks, Samsung Electronics and SK Hynix.\nHowever, concerns that the chip sector's rally may be overdone saw Samsung shares slide 6.1% and SK Hynix's lose 7.5% on Wednesday.",
